HST Office: the office starts when its COM automation component cannot be loaded.

On Windows, every start registers the office's COM class factories by creating
com.sun.star.bridge.OleApplicationRegistration (oleautobridgelo.dll) and
com.sun.star.comp.ole.EmbedServer. Nothing caught a failure there: when Windows refused to load
oleautobridgelo.dll (the file quarantined or blocked on that PC), the CannotActivateFactoryException
left the start-up user event unhandled and the office crashed a few seconds after every start,
before any document could be opened (error report: C++ exception e06d7363 from cppuhelper's
"loading component library <...> failed", called from Desktop::OpenClients_Impl).

Both registrations are optional for working with documents (they let other programs drive the
office or embed its objects), so a failure is now logged and the start goes on; each one is tried
on its own.

License: modified upstream files keep their license (MPL-2.0).
---
--- a/desktop/source/app/app.cxx
+++ b/desktop/source/app/app.cxx
@@ -2002,8 +2002,20 @@
         vcl::fileregistration::CheckFileExtRegistration(SfxGetpApp()->GetTopWindow());
     // Registers a COM class factory of the service manager with the windows operating system.
     Reference< XMultiServiceFactory > xSMgr=  comphelper::getProcessServiceFactory();
-    xSMgr->createInstance("com.sun.star.bridge.OleApplicationRegistration");
-    xSMgr->createInstance("com.sun.star.comp.ole.EmbedServer");
+    // HST Office: COM automation and embedding are optional; a component Windows does not load
+    // (quarantined, blocked) must not end every start with an unhandled exception
+    for (const char* pService : { "com.sun.star.bridge.OleApplicationRegistration",
+                                  "com.sun.star.comp.ole.EmbedServer" })
+    {
+        try
+        {
+            xSMgr->createInstance(OUString::createFromAscii(pService));
+        }
+        catch (const css::uno::Exception&)
+        {
+            TOOLS_WARN_EXCEPTION("desktop.app", "no COM registration: " << pService);
+        }
+    }
 #endif
     const char *pExitPostStartup = getenv ("OOO_EXIT_POST_STARTUP");
     if (pExitPostStartup && *pExitPostStartup)
